\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Introduction\cb1 \

\fs32 \cf10 \cb3 In this lab session, we will set up SonarQube on an EC2 machine and learn how to analyze the code quality of a Java application locally. We will use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-petclinic"}}{\fldrslt 
\f0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf11 Spring PetClinic}} as our sample project.\cb1 \

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Pre-Requisite\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
AWS Account\cf12  \cf10 IAM user with valid permissions\cf12  \cf10 An EC2 Machine (Linux-based) with Docker installed\cf12 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 \cb3 Tasks\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 \cb3 TASK 1 - Setup SonarQube\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Create or use an existing EC2 instance with Docker installed. 
\f2\b Important note:
\f1\b0  A t2.micro or t3.micro is not enough for SonarQube to run normally. You need an EC2 instance of type 
\f2\b t2.medium
\f1\b0  or 
\f2\b t3.medium
\f1\b0  (something with at least 4GB of RAM).\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 Run the following command to start the SonarQube container. This will pull the latest SonarQube image from Docker Hub if not already present:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf13 \cb3 docker\cf14  run\cf15  -d --name\cf14  sonarqube\cf15  \\\cf10 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  -e\cf14  SONAR_ES_BOOTSTRAP_CHECKS_DISABLE=\cf15 true \\\cf10 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cf15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  -p\cf14  9000:9000 sonarqube:latest\cf10 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f3\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cb17 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf10 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\b \cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
-d\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 runs the container in detached mode. 
\f2\b --name sonarqube\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 names the container \'93sonarqube\'94. 
\f2\b -e SONAR_ES_BOOTSTRAP_CHECKS_DISABLE=true\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 disables bootstrap checks (for demo setups). 
\f2\b -p 9000\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 exposes SonarQube on port 9000.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Wait a few moments for SonarQube to fully start. Then, access the SonarQube UI in your browser at: 
\f3 http://<EC2-instance-Public-IP>:9000
\f1  
\f4\i (Default credentials are 
\f5 admin/admin
\f4 .)
\f1\i0 \cf12 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 \cb3 TASK 2 - Scan Java code to generate a Sonar report\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf10 \cb3 We will use the 
\f4\i Spring PetClinic
\f1\i0  project to showcase how to run a code analysis. Below are two approaches:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf2 \cb3 Approach A: Local Analysis via Maven\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
On your local machine (or on your EC2 instance), clone the Spring PetClinic repository:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf13 \cb3 git\cf14  clone https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-petclinic.git\cf10 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
cd\cf14  spring-petclinic\cf10 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f3\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cb17 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf10 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 Ensure you have Java installed (version 17 or newer is recommended). If Maven is not installed, you can use PetClinic\'92s included Maven wrapper (
\f3 mvnw
\f1  on Unix or 
\f3 mvnw.cmd
\f1  on Windows).\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 On Unix-like systems, make the wrapper executable:\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf13 \cb3 chmod\cf14  +x mvnw\cf10 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f3\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cb17 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf10 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 Create a new project in SonarQube:\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1\cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Log in to your SonarQube instance. Go to 
\f2\b Projects\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 > 
\f2\b Create new project\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 . Provide a 
\f2\b Project key\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 and 
\f2\b Display name\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 , then click 
\f2\b Set Up\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b0 \cb3 . Under 
\f4\i Provide a token\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\i0 \cb3 , select 
\f4\i Generate a token\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\i0 \cb3 , name it, generate it, and save it securely.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the SonarQube UI, pick the 
\f2\b Maven
\f1\b0  option and run the command shown (example below):\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cf13 \cb3 ./mvnw\cf14  clean verify sonar:sonar\cf15  \\\cf10 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  -Dsonar.projectKey=YourProjectKey \\\cf10 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cf15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  -Dsonar.host.url=http://\cf18 <\cf15 EC2-instance-Public-IP\cf18 >\cf15 :9000 \\\cf10 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cf15 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
  -Dsonar.login=\cf18 <\cf15 YourGeneratedToken\cf18 >\cf10 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f3\fs32 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 Copy\AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf16 \uc0\u8232 \cb17 Explain\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf10 \cb3 \uc0\u8232 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \cb3 Replace 
\f3 YourProjectKey
\f1  and the token accordingly.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 Once the analysis completes, return to the SonarQube UI to see code quality results.\cf12 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f4\i \cf10 \cb3 (Note: You can adjust Maven goals as needed, e.g., 
\f5 ./mvnw package sonar:sonar
\f4 .)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\i0\fs36 \cf2 \cb3 Approach B: GitHub Actions Analysis 
\f4\i (Optional - takes a little more time)
\f1\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf10 \cb3 If you want to integrate SonarQube scans into CI/CD:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Go to your GitHub repository \uc0\u8594  
\f2\b Settings
\f1\b0  \uc0\u8594  
\f2\b Secrets and variables
\f1\b0  \uc0\u8594  
\f2\b Actions
\f1\b0 , and add two secrets:\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3 \cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
SONAR_HOST_URL\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 \uc0\u8594  
\f3 http://<EC2-instance-Public-IP>:9000\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 SONAR_TOKEN\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cb3 \uc0\u8594  Your token from SonarQube\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf10 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
